id: pm-ka6d
title: Document the measured canonical agent cold-start across docs and generated guidance
description: "Standardize the lowest-token equivalent cold-start protocol across agent docs and generated guidance, with a completed-task replay gate that rejects a more expensive canonical choice."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: agent-ux,"area:docs",simplification
created_at: "2026-07-11T16:23:07.560Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-01T07:49:51.418Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-01T07:49:50.929Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-01T07:49:50.929Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Agent-facing docs name the measured canonical cold-start; generated AGENTS and CLAUDE guidance teaches the same sequence; no new top-level CLI commands are introduced; the fixed 101-item replay reports every compared protocol and fails when the documented canonical protocol is not the lowest-token equivalent choice
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "Replaced opaque JSON-string payload drift reporting with the first RFC 6902 operation and JSON Pointer, added a TDD regression assertion, preserved exact parity semantics, and retained independently observable orientation contracts."
expected_result: Any baseline/accounted application-payload drift fails closed with a compact field-level location; the complete release preflight remains deterministic and exact.
actual_result: "The focused 39-test file, five repeated 21-step replays, 75-test linked cohort, and full 8,239-test preflight passed; exact coverage is 100/100/100/100 and all release gates are green."
