  "2026-09-01T06:46:35.390Z","harness:codex","Review round 17 test-quality evidence: decomposed the oversized orientation selection case into independently named selection, malformed evidence, reference integrity, completeness, normalization, deterministic ordering, duplicate-ID, and invalid-capability contracts. No assertions or negative domains were removed; the focused file passes 39 tests."
  "2026-09-01T06:56:49.614Z","harness:codex","Review round 17 exact coverage: the independently observable orientation contracts are included in the 594-file, 8,239-test repository pass at exact 100/100/100/100; the linked orientation/init cohort also passed 75 tests."
  "2026-09-01T07:19:48.971Z","harness:codex","Failure evidence: pnpm verify:preflight completed static and integration stages, then exact coverage failed 1/8,239 tests because the real-transport replay reported a baseline/accounted application-payload mismatch in assertTransportPayloadParity. The same cohort passed in isolation, so this item is reopened to make the mandatory gate reproducible under full-suite execution; no other pm item is in progress."
  "2026-09-01T07:31:49.543Z","harness:codex","TDD and reproduction evidence: added a failing contract that required payload parity refusals to identify the first JSON Patch operation and pointer; the pre-change test emitted only a generic mismatch. The implementation now retains fail-closed exact parity while reporting a compact op:path diagnostic. The focused 39-test gate and five sequential 21-step standalone replays passed. Repository coverage then passed all 594 files and 8,239 tests, including the previously intermittent real-transport replay, and exposed one honest uncovered formatting fallback; that fallback was removed rather than excluded or artificially exercised. Full preflight remains required before closure."
  "2026-09-01T07:49:50.383Z","harness:codex","Terminal evidence: pnpm verify:preflight passed end to end after 15+ minutes. The replay completed under repository-wide concurrency; all 594 files and 8,239 tests passed at exact 60,643/60,643 statements, 45,850/45,850 branches, 12,619/12,619 functions, and 58,388/58,388 lines. ESLint, zero-duplicate gates, TypeScript surfaces, package/SDK parity, refusal/token/graph/record assurance, secret scanning, packed npx/bunx across 13 packages, 88-command package-first dogfood, and every release gate passed."
